1
00:00:02,180 --> 00:00:05,100
=The Truth (Season 4)=
(Behind-the-Scenes Cast Interview)

2
00:00:05,520 --> 00:00:05,830
Hi, everyone.

3
00:00:05,840 --> 00:00:07,830
(Bai Qichen as Designer Bai)
I play Designer Bai on The Truth Season 4.

4
00:00:07,840 --> 00:00:09,110
I'm Bai Qichen.

5
00:00:09,180 --> 00:00:10,970
Do you play escape rooms a lot?

6
00:00:10,970 --> 00:00:12,540
Now that you know the set,

7
00:00:12,540 --> 00:00:13,730
would you still be scared playing it?

8
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:16,950
I play them all the time.

9
00:00:16,960 --> 00:00:18,310
I usually...

10
00:00:18,320 --> 00:00:19,470
keep a pretty level head.

11
00:00:19,480 --> 00:00:21,670
(Scared but hooked)
But I still get scared and scream.

12
00:00:23,580 --> 00:00:25,700
If you could pick one player
for an escape room,

13
00:00:25,700 --> 00:00:26,440
who would you choose?

14
00:00:26,440 --> 00:00:27,000
Why?

15
00:00:27,680 --> 00:00:29,150
I'd pick

16
00:00:29,150 --> 00:00:30,000
Li Fei.

17
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:31,630
He's always so calm.

18
00:00:31,640 --> 00:00:33,300
Unmoved by gain or loss, joy or sorrow.

19
00:00:33,300 --> 00:00:34,260
(Cracks himself up)

20
00:00:34,260 --> 00:00:35,390
For the next shoot,

21
00:00:35,390 --> 00:00:37,300
what new role or twist
would you want to try?

22
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:39,030
Next time, I want

23
00:00:39,040 --> 00:00:40,150
to join them as a player.

24
00:00:40,160 --> 00:00:41,910
(Let me play too)
I want to see for myself

25
00:00:41,920 --> 00:00:43,870
(Front-row seat to the action)
if they're really that smart.

26
00:00:43,870 --> 00:00:46,770
Pitch this episode
to viewers in one line.

27
00:00:46,770 --> 00:00:47,610
What would you say?

28
00:00:48,080 --> 00:00:49,790
Does this show even need a pitch?

29
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:50,630
(Absolute banger)
Just look at this show.

30
00:00:50,640 --> 00:00:52,070
The production, the cast.

31
00:00:52,080 --> 00:00:53,150
It's good. Go watch it.

32
00:00:53,880 --> 00:00:55,230
(Zhou Jinglin as the Investigator)
I'm Zhou Jinglin.

33
00:00:55,240 --> 00:00:56,310
I'm an actor.

34
00:00:56,310 --> 00:00:58,790
Anything funny happen during filming?

35
00:00:58,800 --> 00:01:00,630
When I showed up,

36
00:01:00,640 --> 00:01:03,210
one of the players said something to me.

37
00:01:03,210 --> 00:01:05,550
The lights were flickering then.

38
00:01:05,560 --> 00:01:07,110
They weren't fully on.

39
00:01:07,120 --> 00:01:08,910
So in that dark room,

40
00:01:08,920 --> 00:01:10,030
when they saw me,

41
00:01:10,040 --> 00:01:10,870
I don't remember who said it.

42
00:01:10,880 --> 00:01:12,750
I think it was Zhang Linghe
or Zhou Keyu.

43
00:01:12,760 --> 00:01:13,350
They said

44
00:01:13,360 --> 00:01:14,630
I'm quite handsome.

45
00:01:14,640 --> 00:01:15,990
(That stuck with me)
I thought that was hilarious.

46
00:01:16,540 --> 00:01:17,640
For the next shoot,

47
00:01:17,640 --> 00:01:19,550
what new role or twist
would you want to try?

48
00:01:19,680 --> 00:01:21,310
I'd love to play a villain.

49
00:01:21,320 --> 00:01:22,510
(New role, new experience)
Try something different

50
00:01:22,520 --> 00:01:25,510
and get more chances

51
00:01:25,520 --> 00:01:26,670
to interact with the players.

52
00:01:27,110 --> 00:01:29,030
Do you usually
play mystery escape rooms?

53
00:01:29,030 --> 00:01:31,640
Now that you know the set,
would it still scare you?

54
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:33,990
I rarely play these games.

55
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:35,670
I've basically never played one.

56
00:01:35,680 --> 00:01:37,950
(Still a newbie)
My brain probably

57
00:01:37,960 --> 00:01:39,190
doesn't work that fast.

58
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:40,750
I'm not great

59
00:01:40,760 --> 00:01:42,150
at solving mysteries.

60
00:01:42,160 --> 00:01:43,590
If I played again,

61
00:01:43,600 --> 00:01:44,870
I'd probably still be scared.

62
00:01:44,880 --> 00:01:46,900
I'm kind of a scaredy-cat.

63
00:01:46,900 --> 00:01:47,820
(Important detail)

64
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:51,930
If you could team up with one player,
who and why?

65
00:01:52,240 --> 00:01:54,030
I'd definitely pick

66
00:01:54,040 --> 00:01:54,950
Liu Yuning.

67
00:01:54,960 --> 00:01:56,510
I think

68
00:01:56,520 --> 00:01:57,750
he's the mastermind.

69
00:01:57,760 --> 00:01:58,790
(Ace detective)
He's the brains of the team.

70
00:01:58,790 --> 00:02:01,530
Pitch this episode
to viewers in one line.

71
00:02:01,530 --> 00:02:02,400
What would you say?

72
00:02:02,480 --> 00:02:03,710
I'd definitely say

73
00:02:03,720 --> 00:02:05,430
this episode is a total banger.

74
00:02:05,440 --> 00:02:05,950
Why?

75
00:02:05,960 --> 00:02:07,150
(Banger of all bangers)
Because I'm the investigator.

76
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:08,780
(Shi Zhongyuan & Sui Xin as school bullies)
In this episode,

77
00:02:08,780 --> 00:02:10,590
what scene stuck with you most?

78
00:02:10,600 --> 00:02:11,430
For me,

79
00:02:11,440 --> 00:02:13,830
it was the scene we did
with Ding Chengxin.

80
00:02:13,840 --> 00:02:14,750
At that moment,

81
00:02:14,760 --> 00:02:16,910
I could really see

82
00:02:16,920 --> 00:02:18,710
the emotion in his eyes.

83
00:02:18,710 --> 00:02:19,100
Yeah.

84
00:02:19,120 --> 00:02:20,550
The emotion felt completely real.

85
00:02:20,560 --> 00:02:22,790
(Hit me right in the heart)
It really made my chest

86
00:02:22,790 --> 00:02:23,980
tighten up.

87
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:27,510
One funny thing was,

88
00:02:27,520 --> 00:02:28,990
while we were waiting for our scene,

89
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:30,070
we were super nervous.

90
00:02:30,080 --> 00:02:33,030
We could hear them

91
00:02:33,040 --> 00:02:36,670
coming into the set,

92
00:02:36,680 --> 00:02:37,390
saying

93
00:02:37,400 --> 00:02:38,350
how much fun it was.

94
00:02:38,360 --> 00:02:40,990
Meanwhile, I was super nervous.

95
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:42,630
(Nervous backstage)
And they kept saying how much fun it was

96
00:02:42,640 --> 00:02:44,110
and how awesome that part was.

97
00:02:44,120 --> 00:02:45,150
And that actually

98
00:02:45,160 --> 00:02:48,030
(Instant relief)
helped me relax a little.

99
00:02:48,030 --> 00:02:48,490
Yeah.

100
00:02:48,550 --> 00:02:50,140
After filming so many episodes,

101
00:02:50,140 --> 00:02:52,110
which scene has stayed with you most?

102
00:02:52,840 --> 00:02:54,030
For me, probably

103
00:02:54,040 --> 00:02:55,790
the Longdong Army.

104
00:02:55,800 --> 00:02:57,310
(Forever a favorite)
Yeah. From where we stood,

105
00:02:57,320 --> 00:02:58,830
we could see everyone up on the flags,

106
00:02:58,840 --> 00:02:59,390
and all those...

107
00:02:59,400 --> 00:03:00,550
Longdong Army!

108
00:03:00,560 --> 00:03:02,230
Those scenes play out.

109
00:03:02,240 --> 00:03:02,990
As an actor,

110
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:05,030
I couldn't help but feel

111
00:03:05,040 --> 00:03:06,310
a little moved by it.

112
00:03:06,320 --> 00:03:08,070
(Moved by the Longdong spirit)
For me,

113
00:03:08,080 --> 00:03:08,790
the most memorable scene

114
00:03:08,800 --> 00:03:10,180
was also the Longdong Army scene.

115
00:03:10,180 --> 00:03:11,420
Because

116
00:03:11,440 --> 00:03:14,190
there were so many actors in it.

117
00:03:14,200 --> 00:03:15,790
And

118
00:03:15,800 --> 00:03:16,510
it was already really late,

119
00:03:16,520 --> 00:03:18,430
but everyone still shouted

120
00:03:18,440 --> 00:03:19,470
that slogan with so much energy.

121
00:03:19,480 --> 00:03:20,270
Besides,

122
00:03:20,280 --> 00:03:21,590
(Fully in character)
while we were performing,

123
00:03:21,600 --> 00:03:23,350
you could see the casts

124
00:03:23,360 --> 00:03:26,790
(Caught up in the moment)
were genuinely moved too.

125
00:03:26,800 --> 00:03:30,150
It was a really powerful scene.

126
00:03:30,160 --> 00:03:30,790
Yeah.

127
00:03:30,790 --> 00:03:33,210
If you could pick one player
for a horror escape room,

128
00:03:33,210 --> 00:03:34,050
who would you choose?

129
00:03:34,050 --> 00:03:34,730
Why?

130
00:03:35,120 --> 00:03:37,790
A horror escape room?

131
00:03:37,790 --> 00:03:38,770
That's tough.

132
00:03:38,780 --> 00:03:40,230
(Impossible choice)
Really tough.

133
00:03:40,240 --> 00:03:41,550
I'm torn

134
00:03:41,560 --> 00:03:43,190
between Liu Yuning and Zhang Linghe.

135
00:03:43,200 --> 00:03:45,070
Zhang Linghe seems

136
00:03:45,080 --> 00:03:46,190
like the kind of person

137
00:03:46,200 --> 00:03:48,190
who's really fearless.

138
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:48,670
And...

139
00:03:48,670 --> 00:03:49,320
Super brave.

140
00:03:49,320 --> 00:03:49,950
(Respect)
Yeah, really brave.

141
00:03:49,960 --> 00:03:51,070
And Liu Yuning...

142
00:03:51,080 --> 00:03:51,550
Well,

143
00:03:51,560 --> 00:03:53,670
I've seen this firsthand.

144
00:03:53,680 --> 00:03:55,440
(Speaking from experience)
His logic is insanely sharp.

145
00:03:55,440 --> 00:03:55,750
Yeah.

146
00:03:55,760 --> 00:03:56,630
Seriously sharp.

147
00:03:56,640 --> 00:03:59,110
It feels like he can see

148
00:03:59,120 --> 00:04:00,590
the whole episode from the start.

149
00:04:00,600 --> 00:04:01,990
He even knew what I was going to say.

150
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:02,710
That's kind of scary.

151
00:04:02,720 --> 00:04:03,510
Yeah, seriously.

152
00:04:03,510 --> 00:04:06,370
Pitch this episode
to viewers in one line.

153
00:04:06,370 --> 00:04:07,220
What would you say?

154
00:04:07,560 --> 00:04:09,590
I think this episode

155
00:04:09,600 --> 00:04:13,270
has moments

156
00:04:13,280 --> 00:04:15,470
where every viewer

157
00:04:15,480 --> 00:04:16,630
will see a bit of themselves.

158
00:04:17,600 --> 00:04:19,750
So yeah.

159
00:04:19,760 --> 00:04:20,710
Don't miss this one.

160
00:04:22,270 --> 00:04:23,100
(Summer as AI Mom, Taiwei as AI Dad)
As the parents, what was it like

161
00:04:23,100 --> 00:04:26,340
seeing six gorgeous,
grown-up kids walk in?

162
00:04:26,340 --> 00:04:27,400
How did that feel?

163
00:04:28,160 --> 00:04:29,430
Honestly? A little intimidating.

164
00:04:29,440 --> 00:04:31,270
Why is everyone so tall?

165
00:04:31,280 --> 00:04:31,910
(Welcome to Giant City)
We felt like

166
00:04:31,920 --> 00:04:33,990
we'd never have kids that tall

167
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:35,830
and that good-looking.

168
00:04:35,840 --> 00:04:36,590
Those genes...

169
00:04:36,600 --> 00:04:37,550
They really hit the genetic jackpot.

170
00:04:39,150 --> 00:04:41,230
They performed the "Leaning Sway"
for you on set.

171
00:04:41,230 --> 00:04:42,480
How would you rate them?

172
00:04:42,800 --> 00:04:43,950
The "Leaning Sway"?

173
00:04:43,960 --> 00:04:45,190
Pretty uneven.

174
00:04:45,200 --> 00:04:47,670
(Fast learners)
But after practice, they looked great.

175
00:04:47,670 --> 00:04:49,110
Who danced it best?

176
00:04:49,280 --> 00:04:49,630
Jin Jing.

177
00:04:49,640 --> 00:04:50,390
Jin Jing was the best.

178
00:04:50,400 --> 00:04:52,070
Who wasn't as good as her?

179
00:04:53,720 --> 00:04:54,710
The online expert.

180
00:04:55,610 --> 00:04:57,810
When you played
the robots glitching out,

181
00:04:57,810 --> 00:04:59,660
what mindset helped you

182
00:04:59,660 --> 00:05:00,720
stay in character?

183
00:05:00,880 --> 00:05:03,350
That... felt pretty normal to me.

184
00:05:03,360 --> 00:05:05,310
Actor commitment. Yeah.

185
00:05:06,620 --> 00:05:09,480
(Summer as AI Mom)
Pitch this episode to viewers in one line.

186
00:05:09,480 --> 00:05:10,380
What would you say?

187
00:05:10,440 --> 00:05:12,630
I think this episode
is going to be great.

188
00:05:12,640 --> 00:05:13,790
It'll keep you guessing.

189
00:05:13,800 --> 00:05:15,790
(High-stakes story)
Everyone was totally locked in,

190
00:05:15,800 --> 00:05:18,070
hunting for clues.

191
00:05:18,080 --> 00:05:18,430
And

192
00:05:18,440 --> 00:05:21,190
it ties in really well

193
00:05:21,200 --> 00:05:22,310
with today's AI.

194
00:05:22,320 --> 00:05:23,070
So

195
00:05:23,080 --> 00:05:24,140
if you're into AI, check it out.

196
00:05:24,140 --> 00:05:24,820
(Highly recommended)

197
00:05:25,080 --> 00:05:27,670
If you could pick one player
for an escape room,

198
00:05:27,670 --> 00:05:28,450
who would you choose?

199
00:05:28,450 --> 00:05:28,940
Why?

200
00:05:29,080 --> 00:05:31,270
I'd probably pick Liu Yuning.

201
00:05:31,280 --> 00:05:32,790
While we were glitched out,

202
00:05:32,800 --> 00:05:34,830
we could hear them working
through the mystery.

203
00:05:34,840 --> 00:05:37,310
I thought he was really good at it.

204
00:05:37,320 --> 00:05:37,950
(I saw it firsthand)
And

205
00:05:37,960 --> 00:05:40,110
he's a strong leader too.

206
00:05:40,120 --> 00:05:40,710
Since

207
00:05:40,720 --> 00:05:42,550
(Sold on Liu Yuning)
I'm not great at mysteries,

208
00:05:42,560 --> 00:05:43,710
I need to stick with someone

209
00:05:43,720 --> 00:05:44,750
who knows how to solve them.

210
00:05:45,460 --> 00:05:46,470
In this episode,

211
00:05:46,470 --> 00:05:48,410
what scene stuck with you most?

212
00:05:48,880 --> 00:05:49,990
Probably when all of them

213
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:51,590
(Unforgettable)
performed "Leaning Sway".

214
00:05:51,600 --> 00:05:52,630
Everyone

215
00:05:52,640 --> 00:05:54,190
was having so much fun.

216
00:05:54,200 --> 00:05:55,350
That whole scene

217
00:05:55,360 --> 00:05:56,390
was really entertaining.

218
00:05:58,120 --> 00:05:59,480
Did anything funny happen

219
00:05:59,480 --> 00:06:01,080
during filming?

220
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:02,590
We were playing robots,

221
00:06:02,600 --> 00:06:03,510
and then we glitched out.

222
00:06:03,520 --> 00:06:04,590
We just froze.

223
00:06:04,600 --> 00:06:05,590
Once we stopped moving,

224
00:06:05,600 --> 00:06:07,030
I thought the players were really sweet.

225
00:06:07,040 --> 00:06:08,750
They suggested

226
00:06:08,760 --> 00:06:10,830
putting the robots on the couch

227
00:06:10,840 --> 00:06:13,230
so we could rest for a bit.

228
00:06:13,240 --> 00:06:14,630
(Standby mode)
I thought

229
00:06:14,640 --> 00:06:16,310
(So thoughtful)
they were really sweet.

230
00:06:16,310 --> 00:06:17,430
For the next shoot,

231
00:06:17,430 --> 00:06:19,470
what new role or twist
would you want to try?

232
00:06:19,480 --> 00:06:20,830
A new role?

233
00:06:20,840 --> 00:06:21,710
I'd love to play

234
00:06:21,720 --> 00:06:24,350
the killer, if I could.

235
00:06:24,360 --> 00:06:26,030
(Ready to go bad)
You know, the one who did it.

236
00:06:27,200 --> 00:06:28,310
A full-on villain.

237
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:29,870
Hi, everyone.

238
00:06:29,880 --> 00:06:31,670
(Zhang Liqiu as Grandma)
I'm Zhang Liqiu.

239
00:06:31,680 --> 00:06:33,990
I play the grandma here.

240
00:06:34,560 --> 00:06:36,430
This is your first time
on a variety show.

241
00:06:36,430 --> 00:06:37,180
How does it feel?

242
00:06:37,200 --> 00:06:39,150
It's been quite an experience.

243
00:06:39,160 --> 00:06:40,750
I never realized

244
00:06:40,760 --> 00:06:42,790
a variety show

245
00:06:42,800 --> 00:06:44,630
could be this big.

246
00:06:44,640 --> 00:06:48,510
There were so many monitors
in the control room,

247
00:06:48,520 --> 00:06:48,990
and then

248
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:50,670
so many cameras on set.

249
00:06:50,680 --> 00:06:52,670
At first,

250
00:06:52,680 --> 00:06:54,150
I was a little overwhelmed.

251
00:06:54,160 --> 00:06:57,310
(A little nervous)
Then some of the younger folks

252
00:06:57,320 --> 00:06:58,750
reassured me

253
00:06:58,760 --> 00:06:59,710
not to be nervous.

254
00:06:59,720 --> 00:07:00,550
Everything was taken care of.

255
00:07:00,560 --> 00:07:02,070
I could just act like I normally would

256
00:07:02,080 --> 00:07:03,020
and relax.

257
00:07:03,140 --> 00:07:04,260
(Finally relaxed)

258
00:07:04,280 --> 00:07:05,230
And after that,

259
00:07:05,240 --> 00:07:06,270
I was fine.

260
00:07:06,520 --> 00:07:08,030
The atmosphere here is wonderful.

261
00:07:08,600 --> 00:07:11,630
Everyone's in their early twenties,

262
00:07:11,640 --> 00:07:12,550
guys and girls alike.

263
00:07:12,560 --> 00:07:14,110
They're such good kids

264
00:07:14,120 --> 00:07:15,470
and so responsible.

265
00:07:15,480 --> 00:07:17,750
(Big thumbs-up to the crew)
I feel right at home here.

266
00:07:17,760 --> 00:07:20,270
Even the cold water feels warm.

267
00:07:20,280 --> 00:07:21,310
I really like it here.

268
00:07:21,320 --> 00:07:23,630
I hope

269
00:07:23,640 --> 00:07:24,830
the show is a huge hit.

270
00:07:24,840 --> 00:07:26,270
Then I will be happy too.

271
00:07:28,010 --> 00:07:29,020
(Kong Pengrui as the ruthless boss)
In this episode,

272
00:07:29,020 --> 00:07:30,980
what scene stuck with you most?

273
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:32,710
The one that really stands out

274
00:07:32,720 --> 00:07:34,550
is when I went in
and kicked over their dumplings.

275
00:07:35,800 --> 00:07:36,830
Before that,

276
00:07:36,840 --> 00:07:38,550
I had to psych myself up.

277
00:07:38,560 --> 00:07:39,470
Because honestly,

278
00:07:40,160 --> 00:07:42,830
I felt awful.

279
00:07:42,840 --> 00:07:44,950
(Felt bad about it)
I had to go in, yell at them,

280
00:07:44,960 --> 00:07:46,830
be really nasty and vicious,

281
00:07:46,840 --> 00:07:49,590
then wreck their plate of dumplings.

282
00:07:49,600 --> 00:07:51,470
But the story called for it.

283
00:07:51,480 --> 00:07:53,150
(Fully psyched up)
So I had to prepare myself for it.

284
00:07:53,160 --> 00:07:53,670
And I pulled it off.

285
00:07:55,170 --> 00:07:56,080
Across these episodes,

286
00:07:56,080 --> 00:07:57,820
what scene has stuck with you most?

287
00:07:57,880 --> 00:08:00,870
That Longdong Army moment last episode.

288
00:08:00,880 --> 00:08:03,390
(Everyone loves the Longdong Army)
When they all came out

289
00:08:03,400 --> 00:08:05,590
and everyone started shouting,

290
00:08:05,600 --> 00:08:07,550
that moment suddenly felt so epic.

291
00:08:08,420 --> 00:08:10,980
Anything fun happened during filming?

292
00:08:11,320 --> 00:08:12,430
Honestly, a lot of it was fun.

293
00:08:12,440 --> 00:08:14,830
Just watching everyone

294
00:08:14,840 --> 00:08:16,750
behind the scenes,

295
00:08:16,760 --> 00:08:20,110
rushing to their next cue,

296
00:08:20,120 --> 00:08:20,830
hurrying back and forth,

297
00:08:20,840 --> 00:08:22,510
weaving around each other,

298
00:08:22,520 --> 00:08:24,590
(Tense, but fun)
then getting into position.

299
00:08:24,600 --> 00:08:25,150
That kind of teamwork,

300
00:08:25,160 --> 00:08:27,430
with the directors

301
00:08:27,440 --> 00:08:28,510
guiding us all the way.

302
00:08:28,520 --> 00:08:29,670
They really worked hard.

303
00:08:29,680 --> 00:08:30,590
(Everyone giving it their all)
And honestly,

304
00:08:30,600 --> 00:08:31,910
going through all those scenes

305
00:08:31,920 --> 00:08:33,310
was a lot of fun

306
00:08:33,320 --> 00:08:33,950
and really special.

307
00:08:35,920 --> 00:08:38,190
If you could team up with one player
for an escape room,

308
00:08:38,190 --> 00:08:39,110
who would you choose?

309
00:08:39,110 --> 00:08:39,740
Why?

310
00:08:40,360 --> 00:08:42,470
I'd pick Liu Yuning.

311
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:44,750
(Popular choice)
He's great at seeing the big picture

312
00:08:44,760 --> 00:08:45,790
and keeping

313
00:08:45,800 --> 00:08:48,350
the whole game moving.

314
00:08:48,360 --> 00:08:49,270
He keeps everything on track.

315
00:08:49,280 --> 00:08:51,630
His analysis is incredibly accurate.

316
00:08:51,640 --> 00:08:52,230
He's seriously good.

317
00:08:53,060 --> 00:08:55,820
Pitch this episode
to viewers in one line.

318
00:08:55,820 --> 00:08:56,570
What would you say?

319
00:08:56,600 --> 00:08:57,390
For this episode,

320
00:08:57,400 --> 00:09:00,710
keep some tissues handy

321
00:09:00,720 --> 00:09:01,550
(Friendly warning)
and get ready for a ride.

322
00:09:01,560 --> 00:09:02,750
Because

323
00:09:02,760 --> 00:09:06,590
as you follow the mystery,

324
00:09:06,600 --> 00:09:07,270
you'll laugh out loud

325
00:09:07,280 --> 00:09:10,070
(All the feels)
and maybe shed a few tears too.

326
